  "full_response": "To set up the embedded credentials within the configuration properly, it's important to note that storing sensitive information like passwords directly within configurations is generally discouraged. Instead, it's recommended that you use a secrets management tool like HashiCorp Vault, HashiCorp Consul, or AWS Secrets Manager. However, for demonstration purposes, I'll show you how they would be included in a configuration, and you should take appropriate measures to secure them.\n\n\n**Prometheus Configuration (prometheus.yml):**\n\n```yaml\nglobal:\n  scrape_interval: 15s\n\nscrape_configs:\n  - job_name: 'prometheus'\n    static_configs:\n      - targets: ['localhost:9090']\n\n  - scrape_interval: 5m\n    job_name: 'node'\n    honor_labels: true\n    tls_config:\n      ...\n    static_configs:\n      - targets: ['localhost:9100']\n        params          job_name: prometheus_io_node_exporter\n        relabel_configs:\n          - source_labels: [__address__]\n            regex: '(localhost|127\\.0\\.0\\.1)'\n            replacement: '${1}:9100'\n```\n\n**Grafana Configuration (grafana.ini):**\n\nGrafana doesn’t directly include datasource connection strings in its configuration, since it primarily relies on datasource plugins that have their own configuration files, often in JSON format such as the one below which can be loaded via Grafana's provisioning feature.\n\n\n```json\n{\n  \"apiVersion\": 1,\n  \"datasources\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Prometheus\",\n      \"type\": \"prometheus\",\n      \"url\": \"http://prometheus_server:9090\",\n      \"access\": \"proxy\",\n      \"isDefault\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"InfluxDB Adapter\",\n      \"type\": \"influxdb-adapter\",\n      \"url\": \"http://influxdb_server:8086\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n**InfluxDB Configuration (influxdb_settings.conf):**\n\n```ini\n[influxdb]\nhost = localhost\nport = 8086\n\n[database]\ndbname = your_database\nprefix = your_prefix_  # 'custom_prefix_'\n\n[auth]\ntype = http_auth\ntimeout = 30\ndefault = true\n```\n\nFor embedded credentials, the tutorial configuration won't be able to show sensitive details like credentials. It's assumed that you would create a dedicated secret file and reference it in the dashboard plugins through Grafana's \"secret files\" support.\n\n\nPlease",
